answer:
Metribuzin 42% + Clodinafop-propargyl 12% WG does not have any recommended dose for potato or other vegetable crops; therefore, it should not be sprayed in potato fields. For potato, no safe dose, correct spray time, or application method has been defined for this herbicide combination, and its use may cause crop damage. Although it is effective in controlling grassy weeds such as Phalaris minor and some broad-leaf weeds, its application in potato can lead to leaf burning, stunted plant growth, damage to tubers, and may also leave chemical residues in potatoes, thereby reducing both quality and yield.
PPQS recommended dosage-
1. Ethalfluralin 36.65% w/w EC(36%)- 800 grams mixed with 200 litres of water per acre. PHI-92 or; 
2. Paraquat-dichloride 24% SL 800 mL mixed with 200 litres of water per acre. PHI-100 or;
3. Metribuzin 70% WP- 3 to 4 DAP or post emergence at 300 grams mixed with 300 litres of water per Acre. PHI-30.
Always use herbicides that are specifically recommended for potato, and apply them at the correct dose and crop stage after taking advice from agriculture experts, KVK, or the agriculture department. This helps protect the crop and ensure better yield.
